00:13:52,950 --> 00:13:57,120
I mean, hey, Shakespeare, how about a chase scene once in a while?

261
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:03,800
Hey, guys, dinner's ready.

262
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:03,800
I'm gonna go wash up first.

263
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,000
Thanks.

264
00:14:08,090 --> 00:14:12,850
What do you think? I want his genes for my kid. Those eyes, those cheekbones.

265
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:16,600
Okay, there's enthusiastic, and there's just plain gay.

266
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,900
You don't like him.

267
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,900
I think he's fine.

268
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,310
But we don't know anything real about him.

269
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:27,820
I wish we could get more information.

270
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:27,820
All right, just follow my lead.

271
00:14:28,610 --> 00:14:32,160
You guys have a great place here.

272
00:14:28,610 --> 00:14:32,160
Thanks. I'm crazy about our place.

273
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,120
Hey, speaking of crazy...

274
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:39,250
do you have a history of mental illness in the family?

275
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,790
Uh, no. Although, I did have an uncle who voted for Dukakis.

276
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:48,380
That's really not the kind of thing we're looking for.

277
00:14:50,010 --> 00:14:51,050
Okay.

278
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:55,260
So, um, tell me, how'd you guys meet?

279
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:58,730
Oh, friends first, drunk in London, you know the story.

280
00:14:58,890 --> 00:15:00,600
I've got a better question for you:

281
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:04,310
Do you or any of your blood relatives have diabetes?

282
00:15:06,730 --> 00:15:07,780
No.

283
00:15:08,190 --> 00:15:11,780
Uh, heart disease? Alzheimer's? Gout?

284
00:15:14,070 --> 00:15:16,830
You guys don't have people for dinner a lot, huh?

285
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:19,370
We're just making conversation.

286
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:23,000
Yeah, well, okay. I heard a joke today. It's pretty funny.

287
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:25,920
You know what's not funny? Male pattern baldness.

288
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,300
You guys have shown a lot of interest in me tonight, and I'm flattered...

289
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:35,760
and quite frankly, a little frightened.

290
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:38,220
Can we just talk about something else?

291
00:15:38,390 --> 00:15:39,810
Sure.

292
00:15:38,390 --> 00:15:39,810
All right.

293
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,850
This ravioli's delicious.

294
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:46,270
I notice you're enjoying that ravioli with a beautiful set of teeth.

295
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,320
Did you have braces as a child?

296
00:15:48,570 --> 00:15:50,940
No, I didn't.

297
00:15:48,570 --> 00:15:50,940
Yes!

298
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:56,490
We're teeth people, Zack.

299
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:05,000
Let's just do it. Let's just go over there and see if she heard.

300
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:06,290
Good plan.

301
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:06,290
Okay.

302
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:11,010
What? Where are you going?

303
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:11,010
Oh, I'm sorry, Rachel.

304
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:14,510
I don't have time for your childish games, okay?

305
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,260
I still have to find something incredible to wear...

306
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:20,430
so I can beat Mike at "Who's More Over Who"!

307
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,940
Hey. Hi.

308
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,940
Hey.

309
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:29,570
Where have you been?

310
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:29,570
Trying on clothes.

311
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:34,570
Oh, really? In the dressing room? Well, that's so weird.

312
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:39,990
Phoebe and I were in the dressing room. Gosh, it's just such a small world.

313
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,700
Rachel, I heard you two guys whispering.

314
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:46,000
Oh, God, you did, you heard. Okay, look, let me explain.

315
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,170
There's nothing to explain. I heard you.

316
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:49,670
Phoebe likes Joey.

317
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:55,680
Yeah.

318
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,560
I don't understand it. I mean, Phoebe likes Joey...

319
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,680
and then she's here to buy a dress to impress another guy?

320
00:17:03,850 --> 00:17:08,650
Yeah, that's Phoebe. That's Phoebe. You know, she just wants them all.

321
00:17:08,810 --> 00:17:11,690
It's, like, she's nympho.

322
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,530
Wow!

323
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,530
Yeah.

324
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:18,530
You know, by the way, I heard you tell her not to do anything.

325
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:23,040
Thanks for sticking up for me. God, you are such a nice person.

326
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:25,410
I try.

327
00:17:59,030 --> 00:18:00,740
Oh!

328
00:18:03,410 --> 00:18:08,500
Oh, my God, you really want me to be the keynote speaker?

329
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:11,130
Thank you!

330
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:15,090
You're welcome.

331
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:29,770
Wow! You look...

332
00:18:30,690 --> 00:18:32,940
stop-eating hot!

333
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:37,240
Which is like the highest level of hotness.

334
00:18:39,030 --> 00:18:41,740
Okay, are you sure? Because I am really dreading going to this party.

335
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:42,950
Then don't go.

336
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:46,870
Mike knows I'm coming. If I don't show up, he'll think it's because of him...

337
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:51,830
and then I'm gonna lose face. That's a very serious thing in my culture.

338
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:57,460
All right, then you go to that party, and you pretend to be over Mike.

339
00:18:57,630 --> 00:19:01,180
Afterward, you come to my place and I'll get you good and drunk.

340
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,090
You got it. Okay.

341
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,810
But not on the wine that you made, okay?

342
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:09,890
Because I just don't want to go back to the emergency room.

343
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:20,950
David?

344
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:22,700
Phoebe! Hi.

345
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:25,280
Oh my god

346
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:25,280
Hi.

347
00:19:25,950 --> 00:19:28,290
Wow! You look unbelievable.

348
00:19:28,450 --> 00:19:30,200
Oh, yeah, well...

349
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:33,830
What are you doing here?

350
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,960
Well, I'm back from Minsk. Uh, permanently.

351
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:38,340
Well, what happened?

352
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,340
Remember how I was trying to achieve...

353
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:43,380
the positronic distillation of subatomic particles?

354
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:45,010
Yeah.

355
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:48,720
Well, after eight years of research, I discovered...

356
00:19:48,890 --> 00:19:51,390
that it can't be done.

357
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:53,270
Well...

358
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,770
great that you're back. How are you?

359
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:58,820
Good. Good. Life is good.

360
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:58,820
Good.

361
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:02,820
Well, I'm seeing someone.

362
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:02,820
Oh.

363
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:04,570
Good for you.

364
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:04,570
Yeah.

365
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:09,120
She's also a scientist, so she's very smart and pretty and, um...

366
00:20:09,290 --> 00:20:11,750
It's actually because of you that we're together.

367
00:20:11,910 --> 00:20:14,790
I mean, I saw what you had with that Mike guy...

368
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:17,040
and I just said, "Boy, I want that."

369
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:20,550
Mike and I broke up.

370
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:20,550
You're kidding me.

371
00:20:20,710 --> 00:20:24,840
Because I'm not seeing anybody. I just totally made that up.

372
00:20:25,010 --> 00:20:27,050
Really?

373
00:20:25,010 --> 00:20:27,050
I don't know why, I'm sorry.

374
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:29,850
I guess I just didn't want to lose face.

375
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:32,270
I understand.

376
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:35,850
Yeah. Okay. So then, okay...

377
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:39,940
So we're both living in New York, not seeing anyone.

378
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:42,360
That's so not like us.

379
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:42,360
Yeah, I know.

380
00:20:42,530 --> 00:20:47,070
Well, this is probably a stupid question, seeing that you look like that...

381
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:50,120
but, um, do you have someplace that you need to be right now?

382
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:51,330
Well...

383
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:53,660
No.

384
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:58,580
Well, do you want to get a drink?

385
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:58,580
I'd love to.

386
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:00,710
Great.

387
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:00,710
Okay.

388
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:05,790
Uh, do you smell beets?

389
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:08,640
Oh, all right, stay upwind of me.

390
00:21:10,850 --> 00:21:14,600
Hey, there's Phoebe. Is that Mike she's with?

391
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:17,310
No, that's David.

392
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:20,230
There's a third guy?

393
00:21:20,690 --> 00:21:23,900
Tip of the iceberg.

394
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:28,200
I'm gonna take off now.

395
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:30,910
You're gonna let me go home, aren't you?

396
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:33,450
Sure you don't want to stay a little longer?

397
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:35,750
No, I should get home. I'm kind of tired.

398
00:21:35,910 --> 00:21:37,620
Are you always tired?

399
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:40,670
Because that could be a sign of clinical depression.

400
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:45,130
No, it's tiring to figure out the age at which all my grandparents died.

401
00:21:47,090 --> 00:21:49,090
I'll see you tomorrow.

402
00:21:47,090 --> 00:21:49,090
Okay.

403
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:50,300
Bye.

404
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,930
I think we found our sperm.

405
00:21:54,930 --> 00:21:56,480
He does seem pretty perfect.

406
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:59,020
Yeah? You think so? Should I ask him?

407
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:02,730
No.

408
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,530
Why not? Just because his great-grandmother was obese?

409
00:22:05,690 --> 00:22:08,360
Our kid's gonna get that from you anyway.

410
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:12,700
No, that's not it.

411
00:22:12,870 --> 00:22:17,330
It's just that when we were asking him all those questions before...

412
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:22,420
I just realized I don't care if he is the most perfect guy in the world.

413
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:26,260
He's not you.

414
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:26,260
Yeah, he's better!

415
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:30,090
No, he's not.

416
00:22:30,260 --> 00:22:34,600
If I can't get pregnant with you, then I don't want to get pregnant by him...

417
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,350
or anyone else.

418
00:22:37,730 --> 00:22:41,230
Really? Are you sure?

419
00:22:37,730 --> 00:22:41,230
Yeah, I'm sure.

420
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,810
Thank God, because I don't wanna do this either.

421
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:47,190
I was just doing it because I thought that was what you wanted.

422
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:50,950
I'm the husband. I'm supposed to bring the sperm.

423
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:53,700
That is so sweet.

424
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:55,950
I love you.

425
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:01,710
So you know this leaves us with...

426
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:03,500
Adoption.

427
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:06,210
How do you feel about that?

428
00:23:07,670 --> 00:23:10,300
I think I feel okay about it.

429
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:14,140
Actually, I think I feel really good about it.

430
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,310
Me too.

431
00:23:16,890 --> 00:23:21,230
I wanna find a baby that needs a home, and I wanna raise it with you.

432
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:25,110
And I wanna mess it up in our own specific way.

433
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:30,150
So this is it? We're really gonna adopt?

434
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:31,990
Yeah.

435
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:36,990
Oh, my God! We're gonna be parents!

436
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:36,990
We are gonna be great parents.

437
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:38,410
And it could be soon.

438
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:41,750
I mean, think about it. Right now, somewhere out there...

439
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:44,580
our baby could be being conceived.

440
00:23:44,750 --> 00:23:49,300
Wait. If we're lucky, and we're really, really, really quiet...

441
00:23:49,460 --> 00:23:53,130
we may be able to hear the sound of a condom breaking.

442
00:23:58,970 --> 00:24:00,060
Hey, Zack.

443
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:02,390
Hey, Chandler.

444
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:04,400
I wanted to apologize for last night.

445
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:06,940
I got the feeling we made you uncomfortable.

446
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,270
No, you didn't.

447
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,270
Really?

448
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:10,150
No, you did.

449
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:12,990
My wife and I have some boundary issues.

450
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,280
Sometimes we ask inappropriate questions.

451
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:17,030
We're working on it.

452
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:20,540
Here are the boards for Friday's pitch.

453
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:20,540
Thank you.

454
00:24:22,790 --> 00:24:26,500
You wouldn't know if she's planning on keeping her baby, would you?

